Well, the vicar's maid cleans the place,

00:59:36.520 --> 00:59:40.210
and the colonel had threatened a chocolate archer bloke back in Chokey for poaching.

00:59:40.210 --> 00:59:44.030
He was only out on parole, and he had a bad time in sight, they say.

00:59:44.030 --> 00:59:47.010
Well, according to village gossip,

00:59:47.010 --> 00:59:50.280
archer's having a bit of a thing with the maid of the vicarage.

00:59:50.280 --> 00:59:53.510
Is he, by God?

00:59:53.510 --> 00:59:55.570
Right.

01:00:02.270 --> 01:00:05.760
Vicar left at when? 5:35? Good.

01:00:05.760 --> 01:00:06.660
About then.

01:00:06.660 --> 01:00:09.050
What do you mean about? It's very important to be precise.

01:00:09.050 --> 01:00:12.170
Well, I didn't know anyone was coming to shoot the old swine, did I?

01:00:12.170 --> 01:00:13.160
Didn't you?

01:00:13.160 --> 01:00:14.440
And what does that mean?

01:00:14.440 --> 01:00:15.620
We'll come to that in a minute.

01:00:15.620 --> 01:00:18.020
No, we won't. We'll come to it now. What do you mean?

01:00:18.020 --> 01:00:20.020
Yes, Inspector. Do you have this specific charge?

01:00:20.020 --> 01:00:22.380
I'll manage, thank you, Vicar.

01:00:22.380 --> 01:00:23.760
And what do you mean?

01:00:23.760 --> 01:00:26.040
You know what I mean.

01:00:26.040 --> 01:00:30.000
There is a certain man with whom you are conducting a certain relationship.

01:00:30.000 --> 01:00:33.210
- If you're talking about Bill Archer, you say so.

01:00:33.210 --> 01:00:37.060
Yes, I know him, and better than most.

01:00:37.060 --> 01:00:40.910
- Better than most.

01:00:40.910 --> 01:00:47.210
Have you got a note of that, Lake?

01:00:47.210 --> 01:00:49.410
- You realize that Mrs. Price Ridley saw Archer

01:00:49.410 --> 01:00:52.470
arrive at the vicarage the night before the murder,

01:00:52.470 --> 01:00:53.650
at past midnight?

01:00:53.650 --> 01:00:55.010
- The old crow.

01:00:55.010 --> 01:00:58.290
- Saw him let into the kitchen, didn't see him leave.

01:01:00.160 --> 01:01:02.390
He hurt himself, didn't he?

01:01:02.390 --> 01:01:05.250
He needed help.

01:01:05.250 --> 01:01:09.120
He had a bad fall, tripped over some sort of cord

01:01:09.120 --> 01:01:12.060
in the woods there, buried it was in the leaves.

01:01:12.060 --> 01:01:13.080
What woods?

01:01:13.080 --> 01:01:14.910
By the vicarage here.

01:01:14.910 --> 01:01:16.430
So he saw a light, so--

01:01:16.430 --> 01:01:18.370
What was he doing in the woods?

01:01:18.370 --> 01:01:19.550
Rabbiting.

01:01:19.550 --> 01:01:21.010
What do you think?

01:01:21.010 --> 01:01:24.650
He wasn't shooting magistrates anyway.

01:01:24.650 --> 01:01:29.600
I gave him a cup of tea, vicar.

01:01:30.190 --> 01:01:32.330
We'd better check in I suppose.

01:01:32.330 --> 01:01:33.830
Detail from Pringle.

01:01:33.830 --> 01:01:34.740
Inspector!

01:01:34.740 --> 01:01:38.010
I believe I have information vital to your investigation.

01:01:38.010 --> 01:01:39.510
Lake!

01:01:39.510 --> 01:01:45.240
Fletcher! Pringle!

01:01:45.240 --> 01:01:51.320
Madam, what can we do for you?

01:01:51.320 --> 01:01:53.320
There was a man in my shrubbery.

01:01:53.320 --> 01:01:57.220
I distinctly heard him sneeze.

01:01:57.220 --> 01:01:58.160
Yes, madam.

01:02:01.820 --> 01:02:04.640
I've considerably revised my opinion of Mary.

01:02:04.640 --> 01:02:05.980
really?

01:02:05.980 --> 01:02:09.040
the way she stood up to Inspector Slack was magnificent.

01:02:09.040 --> 01:02:12.030
no wonder we're a free country.

01:02:12.030 --> 01:02:15.290
this was sent down by Ian Prothero.

01:02:15.290 --> 01:02:19.670
dear Vicar I wonder if you and Griselda would come up and see me as soon as possible.

01:02:19.670 --> 01:02:23.430
I should be very grateful. something very strange has occurred.

01:02:23.430 --> 01:02:26.440
and I should like some advice. yours etc.

01:02:30.030 --> 01:02:30.870
It's a nice evening.

01:02:33.830 --> 01:02:34.750
Let's cycle up.

01:02:41.650 --> 01:02:43.860
There she goes.

01:02:44.800 --> 01:02:45.300
Tear him up.

01:02:45.760 --> 01:02:46.600
Knees down.

01:03:04.860 --> 01:03:07.460
- Good afternoon, ladies.

01:04:12.830 --> 01:04:14.090
I won't be long, Mrs. Salisbury.

01:04:14.650 --> 01:04:15.890
So you'll want your tea, then?

01:04:15.890 --> 01:04:18.370
Please, please. I'm just popping round to Dr. Haydock's.

01:04:30.120 --> 01:04:31.320
- Boris, sorry. - Hello.

01:04:31.320 --> 01:04:35.230
- How are you? - Oh, well, you know.

01:04:35.230 --> 01:04:49.070
- Quite. - There's nothing wrong there.

01:04:49.070 --> 01:04:52.470
Yes, but Dolce has nothing to worry about, Mr. Hawes.

01:04:52.470 --> 01:04:59.380
Now, tell me.

01:05:00.000 --> 01:05:02.720
How exactly does your difficulty in sleeping manifest itself?

01:05:03.320 --> 01:05:05.510
Well, it's not really me, Doctor.

01:05:05.690 --> 01:05:07.350
It's my landlady and her friend.

01:05:07.450 --> 01:05:08.190
They talk.

01:05:08.640 --> 01:05:10.050
I can hear them through the wall.

01:05:10.250 --> 01:05:12.830
I hear snatches of what they're actually saying,

01:05:12.910 --> 01:05:14.970
but whenever I hear my name and try to listen,

01:05:15.430 --> 01:05:17.110
they whisper and I can't hear a thing.

01:05:17.390 --> 01:05:18.470
And this goes on at night?

01:05:18.780 --> 01:05:20.450
Yes, only at night.

01:05:20.750 --> 01:05:22.790
It usually starts as soon as I try to go to sleep.

01:05:24.330 --> 01:05:24.570
Hmm.

01:05:26.330 --> 01:05:29.380
I'm going to prescribe you some powders which are a bit of a relaxant.

01:05:29.730 --> 01:05:30.000
Right.

01:05:30.440 --> 01:05:31.820
they'll help you to feel drowsy.

01:05:33.000 --> 01:05:34.740
But I want you to come back at the end of next week,

01:05:34.980 --> 01:05:36.120
whether they work or not.

