01:16:45.910 --> 01:16:52.150
Wouldn't it be simple if I had?

01:17:28.570 --> 01:17:29.860
Goodhouse from Mattins.

01:18:00.000 --> 01:18:10.530
text today is taken from Psalm 15. Lord, who shall rest on thy holy hill, even he

01:18:10.530 --> 01:18:19.520
that hath used no deceit in his tongue, and hath not slandered his neighbor. My

01:18:19.520 --> 01:18:25.950
friends, we are all, in the meaning of that text, neighbors. Amongst us are some

01:18:25.950 --> 01:18:30.000
who are pure in heart, who will hear with sorrow what I have

01:18:30.000 --> 01:18:35.550
have to say, urging themselves in imitation of God's great son to

01:18:35.550 --> 01:18:43.430
forgiveness of those whom I address, amongst whom I include myself. An act of

01:18:43.430 --> 01:18:47.670
horrible violence and cruelty has taken place amongst us my neighbors, and

01:18:47.670 --> 01:18:53.540
whatever we should discover the reason finally to be, I believe that this was no

01:18:53.540 --> 01:19:00.000
mere accidental occurrence. The ground was prepared, the time was right

01:19:00.000 --> 01:19:07.850
for such a deed we are almost all of us involved and those who are involved are

01:19:07.850 --> 01:19:14.520
guilty and I beg you do not look at it with mundane eyes with the eyes of pity

01:19:14.520 --> 01:19:21.660
justification of everyday excuses look at it with the eyes of eternity for one

01:19:21.660 --> 01:19:26.120
day we shall all be judged we shall not be treated like recalcitrant children

01:19:26.120 --> 01:19:30.000
we shall be viewed with the eyes of that eternal

01:19:30.000 --> 01:19:38.580
judge who weighs our actions absolutely. A fog of anger, and I need remind no one here

01:19:38.580 --> 01:19:44.470
that anger is one of the deadly sins. A fog of anger surrounded the murdered man. A fog

01:19:44.470 --> 01:19:50.860
which the bright light of forgiveness may have dispersed. How many of us can say that

01:19:50.860 --> 01:19:57.170
we found in our hearts even a penny candle of forgiveness to light our way through that

01:19:57.170 --> 01:19:59.590
gloom? Few, I suspect.

01:20:00.730 --> 01:20:01.730
And I know I did not.

01:20:04.620 --> 01:20:07.260
There is one among us who has a dark journey to make.

01:20:09.290 --> 01:20:11.870
One who has broken the mightiest of all commandments.

01:20:13.360 --> 01:20:17.800
Let us all pray that this person has already started on his seemingly impossible journey

01:20:17.800 --> 01:20:20.650
towards the light of our Maker's presence,

01:20:21.680 --> 01:20:24.220
which alone can forgive the unforgivable.

01:20:27.090 --> 01:20:28.070
And what of the rest of us?

01:20:31.120 --> 01:20:40.670
From the depths of my contrition, I beg you, join me, journey with me, offer your supplication

01:20:40.670 --> 01:20:47.980
with mine. Call upon our Maker to intercede for our souls, that our sins may not have

01:20:47.980 --> 01:20:53.630
stained them forever. And in the light of that hoped-for forgiveness, let us forgive

01:20:53.630 --> 01:21:00.000
as he shall forgive us, and renounce that which shall surely die.

01:21:00.090 --> 01:21:01.690
damn us if we continue.

01:21:05.110 --> 01:21:07.300
In the name of the Father, the Son, and the Holy Ghost.

01:21:07.560 --> 01:21:07.760
Amen.

