01:23:17.220 --> 01:23:22.190
dear dear. That must be it, mustn't it? That must be the real note. The other was a forgery.

01:23:22.920 --> 01:23:28.650
Oh, yes. This is the last mortal thing he did. Hawes was trying to telephone to confess.

01:23:30.000 --> 01:23:31.280
Christopher Hall was a murderer.

01:23:32.470 --> 01:23:33.050
It's frightening.

01:23:34.050 --> 01:23:37.450
Well, it depends, doesn't it, on what he wanted to confess, too.

01:23:37.850 --> 01:23:42.450
And if he really did want to confess, why did he try to kill himself before doing so?

01:23:44.980 --> 01:23:46.300
If he did...

01:23:46.300 --> 01:23:47.050
Did.

01:23:47.970 --> 01:23:49.560
Tried to kill himself.

01:23:51.140 --> 01:23:52.220
Oh, I'm sorry, my dear.

01:23:52.300 --> 01:23:54.700
I'm just trying to get used to how stupid I've been.

01:23:54.960 --> 01:23:55.730
Get out of the stairs.

01:23:56.790 --> 01:24:00.000
Oh, it's open.

01:24:01.180 --> 01:24:04.660
As if he had taken an overdose of those powders which I see you've given him.

01:24:04.980 --> 01:24:07.080
But I beg you to keep an open mind on that.

01:24:08.040 --> 01:24:11.750
I believe, you see, that it was meant to look like that.

01:24:12.490 --> 01:24:13.130
What do you reckon?

01:24:13.900 --> 01:24:14.480
God knows.

01:24:15.520 --> 01:24:16.390
Possible.

01:24:18.420 --> 01:24:20.240
Anything's possible in this damn business.

01:24:22.300 --> 01:24:23.160
Cure could have done it.

01:24:24.960 --> 01:24:25.820
Doctor could have done it.

01:24:27.600 --> 01:24:29.700
Church cat could have done it as long as I'm concerned.

01:24:32.490 --> 01:24:37.050
There's only one thing about this business that's certain.

01:24:37.050 --> 01:24:43.450
Wherever you turn, this one person will always be there.

01:24:43.450 --> 01:24:45.870
Good evening, Inspector.

01:25:00.000 --> 01:25:02.680
He took poison, whether he meant to or not.

01:25:02.680 --> 01:25:05.360
The tranquilizers I prescribed couldn't have this effect.

01:25:05.360 --> 01:25:07.700
They were muscle relaxants, basically.

01:25:07.700 --> 01:25:10.000
And their color looks slightly wrong.

01:25:10.000 --> 01:25:11.760
I'll get them analyzed.

01:25:11.760 --> 01:25:13.550
Anyway, it's touch and go.

01:25:13.550 --> 01:25:20.240
Excuse me.

01:25:20.240 --> 01:25:21.060
Miss Marple.

01:25:21.060 --> 01:25:23.000
He didn't intend to, Inspector.

01:25:23.000 --> 01:25:26.140
Someone intended him to.

01:25:26.140 --> 01:25:27.690
Who?

01:25:27.690 --> 01:25:30.000
Well, Mrs. Salisbury had a glimpse of the person who visited

01:25:30.000 --> 01:25:34.800
visited Mr. Hawes after dark this evening, rather surreptitiously, she thought.

01:25:35.500 --> 01:25:37.820
She is, thank heaven, an inquisitive body.

01:25:38.500 --> 01:25:39.770
Who was it, Miss Marble?

01:25:40.590 --> 01:25:42.190
The murderer, of course.

01:25:44.720 --> 01:25:47.120
Now, may I propose a little stratagem?

01:26:36.560 --> 01:26:58.100
That's right. That's who I wanted to speak to. There's been a most awful accident, you know. Poor Mr. Horse took his life, they say. Is he dead? Or good as. Won't ever come out of it. They reckon he'll be dead before the night's out.

01:27:01.020 --> 01:27:02.900
They've all gone now, thank goodness.

01:27:05.740 --> 01:27:08.580
Police were here. Everything.

01:27:09.940 --> 01:27:13.970
I didn't tell them that I saw you come round earlier.

01:27:14.350 --> 01:27:16.510
I thought you wouldn't want to be mixed up in it.

01:27:17.120 --> 01:27:22.280
But as you were a friend of poor Mr. Hawes, I thought you'd like to know...

01:30:49.770 --> 01:30:52.840
Oh, well, Mr. Redding.

01:31:30.700 --> 01:31:37.720
There's a note.

01:31:37.720 --> 01:31:43.840
May I see it?

01:31:43.840 --> 01:31:47.600
Oh, thank you, Inspector. Yes, oh dear.

01:31:51.680 --> 01:31:55.130
Why did poor Anne Prothero take her own life?

01:31:55.130 --> 01:31:59.890
Do you think she suspected that Redding had shot Prothero and couldn't live with it?

01:32:00.800 --> 01:32:06.120
- No, no, no, no, what she couldn't live with

01:32:06.120 --> 01:32:09.360
was the fact that she was a murderer.

01:32:09.360 --> 01:32:12.640
She killed her husband, you know.

01:32:12.640 --> 01:32:13.480
- And?

01:32:13.480 --> 01:32:16.920
- Oh, yes, just as she told us she did.

01:32:16.920 --> 01:32:21.550
When, of course, we weren't meant to believe it.

01:32:21.550 --> 01:32:22.630
Is that the time?

01:32:22.630 --> 01:32:25.050
I think I really-- - Miss Marple, you mustn't go.

01:32:25.050 --> 01:32:27.270
You must tell us what happened.

01:32:27.270 --> 01:32:29.000
Where is that wretched girl with the tea?

01:32:37.550 --> 01:32:54.930
- Oh, Vicarage?

01:32:54.930 --> 01:32:56.510
- You'd better get home with their tea, girl.

01:32:56.510 --> 01:32:57.460
- No, I'll hurry.

01:33:10.110 --> 01:33:13.010
you'll be glad to hear that Christopher Hawes has regained consciousness and is

01:33:13.010 --> 01:33:20.750
out of danger. oh thank goodness for that. oh yes indeed yes. now do sit down then we're

01:33:20.750 --> 01:33:26.250
not going to let Miss Marple go to bed until she's explained everything. oh well

01:33:26.250 --> 01:33:30.000
you see I made the most dreadful mistake of underestimating young Mr.

01:33:30.000 --> 01:33:34.700
i thought we were dealing with someone whose crudity would eventually express them

01:33:34.700 --> 01:33:39.240
what i hadn't bargained for was being made to think it was someone not very bright when

01:33:39.240 --> 01:33:45.750
in fact he was extremely subtle the double confession pointing the finger too crudely

01:33:45.750 --> 01:33:51.850
at the real murderer planting the colonel's letter on eccentric mr halls and staging his

01:33:51.850 --> 01:33:56.180
suicide most clever i think we've been extremely lucky inspector

01:33:56.180 --> 01:34:00.000
you see what i still know oh you want to know how they did it

01:34:01.400 --> 01:34:03.910
We have to go back to the morning of the murder.

01:34:03.910 --> 01:34:06.790
Mr. Redding waited till you've gone out, Vicar.

01:34:06.790 --> 01:34:08.520
Griselda was in London.

01:34:08.520 --> 01:34:14.310
It wasn't until you'd rearranged your room, Vicar,

01:34:14.310 --> 01:34:17.160
that I realized where Mr. Redding must have put his gown.

01:34:17.160 --> 01:34:24.790
He'd already immobilized your car, so the scene was now set.

01:34:24.790 --> 01:34:27.940
That evening, Mr. Redding telephoned you,

01:34:27.940 --> 01:34:30.000
pretending to be Mr. Abbott's neighbor.

01:34:30.640 --> 01:34:31.740
And you were out of the way.

01:34:34.770 --> 01:34:36.770
They counted on my being in my garden.

01:34:37.520 --> 01:34:38.660
Good evening, Miss Marple.

01:34:40.370 --> 01:34:42.010
Oh, good evening, Mrs. Prothero.

01:34:42.540 --> 01:34:44.820
The dress was selected with great care.

01:34:45.740 --> 01:34:47.680
She knew I was a noticing sort of person.

01:34:48.320 --> 01:34:51.780
But I could tell she hadn't so much as a handkerchief in the top of her stockings.

01:34:52.550 --> 01:34:53.390
Never mind a gun.

01:34:55.260 --> 01:34:58.070
The gun was silenced.

01:35:00.380 --> 01:35:03.830
But when it went off, Mrs. Price Ridley heard it.

01:35:03.830 --> 01:35:09.030
She believed she'd heard someone in her shrubbery, sneezing, she thought.

01:35:09.030 --> 01:35:13.410
So she went upstairs to get a better view.

01:35:13.410 --> 01:35:18.360
Now, this was very unfortunate, as she was not there to connect the sound of the sneeze

01:35:18.360 --> 01:35:26.200
with Mrs. Protheroe leaving the study and crossing to the studio to await Mr. Redding.

01:35:26.200 --> 01:35:28.870
It was a few minutes before he turned up.

01:35:30.510 --> 01:35:34.550
I nearly missed him, as a matter of fact, as I was at that moment occupied in another

01:35:34.550 --> 01:35:37.640
part of my garden.

01:35:37.640 --> 01:35:42.650
I didn't notice that he was not quite his usual self, but I should have been alerted

01:35:42.650 --> 01:35:44.690
by the fact that he waved to me.

01:35:44.690 --> 01:35:48.700
He'd never done that before.

01:35:48.700 --> 01:35:52.970
He wanted to be noticed, you see.

01:35:52.970 --> 01:35:57.510
Mr. Redding had set up one of the nesting boxes at the edge of the woods with a loudspeaker

01:35:57.510 --> 01:35:58.640
inside it.

01:35:58.640 --> 01:36:00.000
The wire running down.

01:36:00.000 --> 01:36:06.760
back to his tape recorder inside the studio. This was the wire that Bill Archer tripped

01:36:06.760 --> 01:36:14.320
over the night before the murder. At precisely 6.30, Mr. Redding switched on the tape recorder

01:36:14.320 --> 01:36:27.940
and the final touch to this masterpiece of confusion was applied. The shot sounded odd

01:36:27.940 --> 01:36:29.180
so it took my attention.

01:36:30.670 --> 01:36:37.590
Mr. Redding was relying on the fact that a gunshot inside a room, which then echoed outside, would sound odd.

01:36:37.590 --> 01:36:43.080
I don't think Anne Prothero ever recovered from what she'd done.

01:36:44.340 --> 01:36:50.950
Mr. Redding's company, she might have forgotten occasionally, but I think she realised she'd destroyed her life.

01:36:52.370 --> 01:36:54.290
Oh, she had wealth and freedom, of course.

01:36:55.880 --> 01:36:59.340
She tried to save Lawrence Redding to the last.

01:37:01.600 --> 01:37:03.850
Well, I must say, I'm glad you didn't succeed.

01:37:04.770 --> 01:37:05.450
That would never do.

01:37:09.060 --> 01:37:09.460
Tea.

01:37:11.690 --> 01:37:15.640
Oh, and some of your rock cakes.

01:37:15.780 --> 01:37:16.820
How thoughtful of you.

01:37:30.860 --> 01:37:35.500
Oh dear, do you think you should? In your condition?

01:37:35.500 --> 01:37:41.110
I've always suspected you of keeping a broomstick under the stairs, Miss Markle.

01:37:41.110 --> 01:37:43.170
And now I know.

01:37:43.170 --> 01:37:44.490
Griselda?

01:37:44.490 --> 01:37:46.150
Yes, Len, darling.

01:37:46.150 --> 01:37:50.020
Well, I mean... condition?

01:37:50.020 --> 01:37:54.740
A little clement is forecast.

01:37:54.740 --> 01:37:56.000
Oh, I say.

01:37:56.000 --> 01:37:57.440
Yes, but when I still don't see...

01:37:57.440 --> 01:37:58.450
I say!

01:38:00.160 --> 01:38:05.640
What was that?

01:39:09.530 --> 01:39:10.880
Music
